    "items": [
      {
        "id": "o5u83an",
        "kind": "project",
        "title": "Vertex guitar",
        "date": "2026-08-10",
        "image": "a:s9ba9zg",
        "url": "",
        "text": "The Vertex guitar project stems from advanced academic\nresearch conducted as part of a master's thesis in industrial\ndesign. The project focuses on developing a semi-hollow\nelectric guitar that integrates computational design and\ndigital fabrication technologies to achieve optimal acoustic\nperformance. The core innovation of the Vertex guitar lies\nin its generative internal topography and morphological\ndesign. This complex internal structure is engineered to\nphysically eliminate feedback—a common challenge with\nsemi-hollow guitars. By utilizing precise algorithmic\nmodeling for the resonant chamber, the internal geometry\nprevents feedback without compromising the instrument's\nunique tonal qualities. Ultimately, this project demonstrates\nhow merging advanced manufacturing, generative\nalgorithms, and deep acoustic understanding can push the\nboundaries of traditional instrument design.",
        "tags": [
          "Luthiery",
          "Woodworking"
        ]
      },
      {
